  "details": "There's a lot of models, most typically non humanoid ones in desktop mode, where the model frequently clips into the first person camera and obscures significant portions of your screen which can be very disruptive. I feel like a decent fix would be a control slider for the opacity of how you see yourself in first person (mirrors and others are unaffected).\n\nI happened to come across a model that had that and I immediately went like \"this needs to be a global setting!\"",
